#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""earlyoom-kill-watch: tell a session when the host's earlyoom kills one of its processes.

    earlyoom-kill-watch [--to ID] [--dry-run] [--state FILE]      # the service: runs until stopped
    earlyoom-kill-watch --replay --since 2026-11-02T15:00Z [--until ...] [--to ID] [--send]
    earlyoom-kill-watch --counts                                  # kills per hour, as JSON

Why this exists: on 2026-11-02 the host's earlyoom (`earlyoom -m 10,5 -s 100,100 --sort-by-rss
--ignore <omp, tmux, sshd, ...>`) sent SIGTERM 51 times by 15:23Z, 15 of them in the 15:00Z
hour, each time available memory fell to 10%. The kills are by design: they keep the sessions
alive. But a killed tool exits 143 with no message, so its session cannot tell why. RULING
(01a199e0) spent time on that at 15:21Z after its box's `simsci` died four times.

What it does, as one long-running user service (`omp/earlyoom-kill-watch.service`):

  1. Every 2 s it reads /proc/<pid>/stat of every process and records each one with at least
     64 MiB resident: its start time, its name, and the session that owns it. The pid is gone
     once earlyoom has killed it, so the owner must be known BEFORE the kill.
  2. It follows `journalctl -u earlyoom -o json` and, for each `sending SIGTERM to process ...`
     line, finds the owner from step 1, keeps the `mem avail` line just before it, and adds the
     kill to that session's batch.
  3. A batch is sent one minute after its first kill, so several kills of one session in one
     minute are one Envoy notice of at most 600 characters: what was killed, when, its RSS, and
     what to do next. The rest (the host's available memory at each kill, the full command
     lines, how the owner was found) is in the report file the notice names last.
  4. The box-level rate: when more than BOX_RATE (100) kills fall in a rolling hour, matched or
     not, one message goes to the box-health owner -- the `lead-box-health` Envoy role, and the
     SRE session only when nobody holds it. Again only when twice as many kills as it last told
     come after that message (inside an hour), or once the rolling rate has fallen back to 100
     and crosses again. 846 kills in 48 h on sami-rocqperf, 730 of them in the 00Z hour of
     2026-11-03, sent nothing box-level before this; replayed under this rule they are two
     messages (00:40:35Z at 103/h, 00:44:49Z when 214 more had come).
  5. Every minute it logs one line, `kills_this_hour=N hour=YYYY-MM-DDTHHZ kills_prev_hour=M
     unmatched_this_hour=U notices_this_hour=X tracked=T pending=P sample_ms=S box_rate_1h=R`,
     for any reader that wants the rate (`journalctl --user -u earlyoom-kill-watch -g
     kills_this_hour -n 1`).

How the owner is found, best first (the notice says which one matched). "Live here" means
`envoy ps --json` lists the session on this host, or in an agent box (a docker container named as
the box's host) that runs on this host. A systemd scope outlives the session that made it: after a
session moves to another machine or ends, every process left in its scope would otherwise reach a
session that cannot act (2026-11-03 20:28Z: session 01a14126's loky python, left in the chief's
old run-c01a13dcae9797264.scope, reached the chief).

  1. the scope's live omp: the one session `omp` that runs in the process's agent box (docker
     scope) or `run-*.scope` and is still alive.
  2. the process itself: the nearest `omp` ancestor still alive (omp's `__omp_worker*` helpers
     skipped; in an agent box the tool's ancestors run through the box's omp too, since the host
     sees the box's processes with shifted uids, 166536); else the session its environment
     names (`OMP_SESSION_ID`, else the omp pid in `AGENT_SESSION_SCRATCH`), read when it was
     first sampled or while earlyoom's pid still lives, live here; else the one live-here
     session that every other process of its cgroup names in its environment; else a path in
     its command line or working directory: `session-tmp/<omp pid>-XXXXXXXX` (the scratch
     directory scripts/agent-session makes before it execs omp), a full session id (not one in a
     transcript's `Z_<id>` name: a transcript directory names its subagents' parent), or a
     directory `<Name>-<first 8 hex of a session id>` (`/mnt/nvme/sami/tmp/TwoPartStage1-01a14126/`)
     when exactly one live-here session starts so.
  3. a `run-c<16 hex>-svc[-N].scope` whose Description starts `omp session <uuid>`:
     that session, when it is live here. In an
     `omp-broker-<16 hex>[-N].scope` step 2 ignores an environment equal to the broker's own (the
     session that started the broker, which a headless browser inherits), and every environment
     when no broker is left there to compare.
  4. the scope's original session: the session id in a `run-*.scope`'s Description (`omp session
     <uuid> ...`, or shims/omp's `agent-session omp --resume <uuid>`), else the 16 hex of
     `run-c<16 hex>.scope`, only when that session is live here.
  * otherwise, when the process sat in a session's scope (a `run-*.scope`, an agent box, or an
    `omp-broker-*.scope` that serves several sessions): "owner unknown", one notice a minute to
    the box-health owner (the `lead-box-health` role, else the SRE session) with each command
    line, never to a session that moved or ended.
  * otherwise unmatched (system services, containers outside a box, a process never sampled with
    no session path): counted and logged, and nobody is told. The box-level rate covers them.

The session id of an omp: the transcript it holds open (`.../<time>Z_<id>.jsonl`, the same rule
scripts/agentbox uses), else the id in the last path component of its `--resume`/`--restore`
argument (a lane resumed from a subagent's transcript, `.../<time>Z_<parent>/<time>Z_<own>.jsonl`,
is <own>, never <parent>; the same for a scope's Description), else, for a box whose omp
the host cannot read, `docker exec <box>` reading the box omp's open files (only at notice time).

It kills nothing, and changes no limit. earlyoom's own `-N` hook runs after the kill, when the
pid is already gone, and earlyoom's config belongs to agent-infra's guard, so this watch reads
the journal instead.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import fcntl
import json
import os
import pwd
import queue
import re
import signal
import socket
import subprocess
import sys
import threading
import time
from collections import Counter
from pathlib import Path

# A session's own notice goes to that session. The box-level rate goes to the box-health lead's
# Envoy role (dispatch://INFRA-716), and to the SRE session only when nobody holds the role.
BOX_HEALTH_ROLE_TOPIC = "notifications.role.lead-box-health"
SRE = "01a18385-f8c8-74a9-b6ff-694fb5fe87a7"
ENVOY = Path(__file__).resolve().parent / "envoy"
PROC_ROOT = Path("/proc")
_NVME_STATE = Path("/mnt/nvme/sami/tmp/earlyoom-kill-watch/state.json")
DEFAULT_STATE = (
    _NVME_STATE
    if os.access("/mnt/nvme/sami/tmp", os.W_OK)
    else Path(os.environ.get("XDG_STATE_HOME", str(Path.home() / ".local/state"))) / "earlyoom-kill-watch/state.json"
)
# Report files go where every recipient can open them: an agent box binds /mnt/durable/<user>
# whole, and has no /mnt/nvme/<user>/tmp (23 of the 197 notices of 2026-11-02 15:44Z-02:00Z went
# to sessions in boxes).
_DURABLE_TMP = Path("/mnt/durable") / pwd.getpwuid(os.getuid()).pw_name / "tmp"
DEFAULT_REPORTS = (
    _DURABLE_TMP / "earlyoom-kill-watch/reports" if os.access(_DURABLE_TMP, os.W_OK) else DEFAULT_STATE.parent / "reports"
)
MESSAGE_LIMIT = 600  # characters in one Envoy message; the detail goes to the report it names
REPORT_DAYS = 7
BOX_RATE = 100  # kills in a rolling hour, matched or not, that make one box-level message
BOX_WINDOW = 3600.0

SAMPLE_EVERY = 2.0  # seconds between /proc samples
RSS_FLOOR = 64 << 20  # the smallest process worth recording; today's smallest victim had 190 MiB
# How long a vanished process stays in the table. The kill line arrives within seconds of the
# kill, and a restart reads on from its cursor 10 s later. Short, because processes of 64 MiB
# or more churn: 4,268 records in the first six minutes on sami-rocqperf (3,099 of them python3)
# at the first try of 15 minutes.
KEEP_DEAD = 180.0
BATCH = 60.0  # one notice per session per minute of kills
RETRY = 30.0  # wait before a failed send is tried again
STALE = 900.0  # a kill older than this when read is counted, not sent
HOURS_KEPT = 48
PAGE = os.sysconf("SC_PAGE_SIZE")

KILL_RE = re.compile(
    r'^sending (?P<signal>SIG[A-Z]+) to process (?P<pid>\d+) uid (?P<uid>\d+) "(?P<comm>.*?)": '
    r'oom_score (?P<score>-?\d+), VmRSS (?P<rss>\d+) MiB, cmdline "(?P<cmdline>.*?)"?$'
)
AVAIL_RE = re.compile(r"^mem avail: +(\d+) of +(\d+) MiB \( *([0-9.]+)%\)")
UUID = r"[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}"
TRANSCRIPT_RE = re.compile(r"/sessions/.*/[0-9T:-]*Z_(" + UUID + r")\.jsonl$")
# The session id of an omp is the id in the LAST path component of its --resume (or --restore)
# argument: the transcript file's own name. A lane resumed from a subagent's transcript runs
# `--resume .../<time>Z_<parent id>/<time>Z_<own id>.jsonl`; the parent id earlier in the path is
# not its session.
RESUME_ID_RE = re.compile(r"^(?:[0-9T:-]*Z_)?(" + UUID + r")(?:\.jsonl)?$")
SESSION_TMP_RE = re.compile(r"/session-tmp/(\d+)-[A-Za-z0-9]{8}(?:/|\s|$)")
# A session id in a path, not one in a transcript's name (`Z_<id>`): a transcript directory
# holds its subagents' transcripts, so it names their parent, not their owner.
SESSION_UUID_RE = re.compile(r"(?<![0-9a-f])(?<!Z_)(" + UUID + r")(?![0-9a-f])")
# A directory a session names after itself: `<Name>-<first 8 hex of its id>`, e.g.
# /mnt/nvme/sami/tmp/TwoPartStage1-01a14126/. Session ids are UUIDv7 of 2026, so `01`.
SESSION_DIR_RE = re.compile(r"/[A-Za-z][\w.]*-(01[0-9a-f]{6})(?=[/\s\"']|$)")
DOCKER_RE = re.compile(r"/docker-([0-9a-f]{64})\.scope")
SCOPE_RE = re.compile(r"^(.*?/(?:run-[^/]+|session-[^/]+|tmux-spawn-[^/]+|omp-broker-[^/]+)\.scope)")
# systemd 255 adds no process to a running scope without Delegate=yes. Numbered suffixes
# (`<name>-2.scope`, `-3`, ...) share a base scope name for attribution.
RUN_C_RE = re.compile(r"^run-c([0-9a-f]{16})(-svc)?(?:-\d+)?\.scope$")
# omp-broker-<16 hex of sha256(runtime dir)>.scope: omp's shared worker broker, for many sessions.
BROKER_RE = re.compile(r"^omp-broker-([0-9a-f]{16})(?:-\d+)?\.scope$")
DESCRIPTION_RE = re.compile(r"^omp session (" + UUID + r")")
LIVE_TTL = 60.0  # seconds a read of `envoy ps --json` is reused


def log(message: str) -> None:
    print(message, flush=True)


def utc(epoch: float) -> str:
    return time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime(epoch))


def hour_key(epoch: float) -> str:
    return time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%HZ", time.gmtime(epoch))


def resume_session(words: list[str]) -> str:
    """The session id an omp command line resumes: the id in the last path component of its
    `--resume`/`--restore` argument (`<id>`, `<time>Z_<id>.jsonl` or a path ending so), else ""."""
    for i, word in enumerate(words):
        flag, eq, value = word.partition("=")
        if flag in ("--resume", "--restore"):
            value = value if eq else (words[i + 1] if i + 1 < len(words) else "")
            match = RESUME_ID_RE.match(value.rstrip("/").rsplit("/", 1)[-1])
            return match[1] if match else ""
    return ""


def parse_kill(message: str) -> dict | None:
    match = KILL_RE.match(message)
    if not match:
        return None
    return {
        "signal": match["signal"], "pid": int(match["pid"]), "uid": int(match["uid"]), "comm": match["comm"],
        "oom_score": int(match["score"]), "rss_mib": int(match["rss"]), "cmdline": match["cmdline"],
    }


def parse_avail(message: str) -> tuple[int, int, float] | None:
    match = AVAIL_RE.match(message)
    return (int(match[1]), int(match[2]), float(match[3])) if match else None


def message_of(entry: dict) -> str:
    message = entry.get("MESSAGE") or ""
    if isinstance(message, list):  # journald gives non-UTF-8 text as a byte array
        message = bytes(message).decode("utf8", "replace")
    return message


def docker_session(container: str) -> str:
    """The session of the omp in a box, from inside it: the transcript its omp holds open."""
    script = (
        'for p in $(pgrep -x omp); do for fd in /proc/$p/fd/*; do readlink "$fd" 2>/dev/null; done; done'
    )
    try:
        done = subprocess.run(["docker", "exec", container, "sh", "-c", script],
                              capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=15, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return ""
    found = sorted({m[1] for m in map(TRANSCRIPT_RE.search, done.stdout.splitlines()) if m})
    return found[0] if len(found) == 1 else ""


def scope_description(unit: str) -> str:
    """The Description of a user scope. shims/omp starts each host session in `run-*.scope` and
    systemd describes it by its command, `.../agent-session omp --resume <id>`."""
    try:
        done = subprocess.run(["systemctl", "--user", "show", "-p", "Description", "--value", unit],
                              capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return ""
    return done.stdout.strip() if done.returncode == 0 else ""


def local_sessions(host: str) -> dict[str, str]:
    """{session id: host} of every session `envoy ps --json` lists on this host, or in an agent
    box that runs here (Envoy names a box's host as its docker container is named)."""
    try:
        done = subprocess.run([str(ENVOY), "ps", "--json"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60,
                              stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
        rows = json.loads(done.stdout) if done.returncode == 0 else []
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError, ValueError) as error:
        log(f"envoy ps failed: {error}")
        rows = []
    rows = rows if isinstance(rows, list) else (rows.get("sessions") or [])
    here = {host}
    try:
        done = subprocess.run(["docker", "ps", "--format", "{{.Names}}"], capture_output=True, text=True,
                              timeout=30, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
        here |= set(done.stdout.split())
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        pass
    return {r["session_id"]: r.get("host") or "" for r in rows
            if isinstance(r, dict) and r.get("session_id") and r.get("host") in here}


def envoy_send(target: str, text: str) -> bool:
    try:
        done = subprocess.run([str(ENVOY), "send", "--source", "envoy", "--message-file", "-", target],
                              input=text, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as error:
        log(f"send to {target} failed: {error}")
        return False
    if done.returncode != 0:
        log(f"send to {target} failed: exit {done.returncode}: {(done.stderr or done.stdout).strip()}")
    return done.returncode == 0


def meminfo_available(proc_root: Path) -> str:
    try:
        rows = dict(line.split(":", 1) for line in (proc_root / "meminfo").read_text().splitlines())
        avail, total = int(rows["MemAvailable"].split()[0]), int(rows["MemTotal"].split()[0])
    except (OSError, KeyError, ValueError):
        return ""
    return f"{100.0 * avail / total:.1f}% ({avail >> 10} of {total >> 10} MiB)"


def bounded(text: str, tail: str) -> str:
    """`text` then `tail`, at most MESSAGE_LIMIT characters: the tail (the report's path) is kept
    whole and the text cut at its end, so the decision at its start always survives."""
    room = MESSAGE_LIMIT - len(tail)
    if len(text) > room:
        text = text[: max(0, room - 2)].rstrip() + "… "
    return text + tail


def listed(items: list[str], room: int) -> str:
    """As many of `items` as fit in `room` characters, then how many more the report lists."""
    shown: list[str] = []
    for i, item in enumerate(items):
        rest = len(items) - i - 1
        if len("; ".join(shown + [item]) + (f"; and {rest} more" if rest else "")) > room:
            break
        shown.append(item)
    rest = len(items) - len(shown)
    if not rest:
        return "; ".join(shown)
    return "; ".join(shown) + f"; and {rest} more" if shown else f"{rest} kills, each in the report"


class Watch:
    def __init__(self, proc_root: Path = PROC_ROOT, state_path: Path = DEFAULT_STATE, send=envoy_send,
                 to: str = "", host: str = "", docker_session=docker_session, started: float = 0.0,
                 replay: bool = False, describe=scope_description, reports_dir: Path = DEFAULT_REPORTS,
                 live=None) -> None:
        self.proc_root = Path(proc_root)
        self.state_path = Path(state_path)
        self.reports_dir = Path(reports_dir)
        self.send = send
        self.to = to
        self.host = host or socket.gethostname()
        self.docker_session = docker_session
        self.describe = describe
        # The sessions live on this host ({id: host}), read at kill time only and reused LIVE_TTL s.
        self.live = live or (lambda: local_sessions(self.host))
        self._live: dict[str, str] = {}
        self._live_at = -LIVE_TTL
        self.replay = replay
        self.lock = threading.RLock()
        state: dict = {}
        try:
            state = json.loads(self.state_path.read_text())
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            state = {}
        self.cursor: str | None = state.get("cursor")
        self.last_ts: int = int(state.get("last_ts") or 0)
        self.recent: list[str] = list(state.get("recent") or [])
        # A record from before 2026-11-03 holds one owner, not the evidence owner_of weighs at the
        # kill; dropped, its process is sampled again in 2 s.
        self.table: dict[str, dict] = {k: e for k, e in (state.get("table") or {}).items() if "tree" in e}
        self.sessions: dict[str, dict] = state.get("sessions") or {}
        self.hours: dict[str, dict] = state.get("hours") or {}
        self.pending: list[dict] = state.get("pending") or []
        self.avail: list | None = state.get("avail")
        # The box-level rate: every kill of the last two hours as [at, session or "", comm, rss MiB],
        # the storm's state ({"open", "told", "told_at"}), and its message not yet delivered.
        self.box_kills: list[list] = state.get("box_kills") or []
        self.box: dict = state.get("box") or {}
        self.box_pending: dict | None = state.get("box_pending")
        # With no cursor, the journal is read from the hour's start for the count only: a kill
        # from before this watch started is not news.
        self.notify_after = 0.0 if (self.cursor or replay) else started
        self.sample_ms = 0
        self.procs: dict[int, tuple[str, int, int, int]] = {}
        self._omp_cgroups: dict[tuple[int, int], str] | None = None
        self._brokers: dict[str, dict] | None = None

    # ---------------------------------------------------------------- /proc

    def read(self, pid: int, name: str) -> bytes:
        try:
            return (self.proc_root / str(pid) / name).read_bytes()
        except OSError:
            return b""

    def stat(self, pid: int) -> tuple[str, int, int, int] | None:
        """(comm, ppid, start ticks, rss bytes) from /proc/<pid>/stat."""
        text = self.read(pid, "stat").decode("utf8", "replace")
        close = text.rfind(")")
        if close < 0:
            return None
        fields = text[close + 2:].split()
        try:
            return text[text.find("(") + 1:close], int(fields[1]), int(fields[19]), int(fields[21]) * PAGE
        except (IndexError, ValueError):
            return None

    def scan(self) -> dict[int, tuple[str, int, int, int]]:
        procs = {}
        try:
            names = os.listdir(self.proc_root)
        except OSError:
            return procs
        for name in names:
            if name.isdigit():
                row = self.stat(int(name))
                if row:
                    procs[int(name)] = row
        return procs

    def cmdline(self, pid: int) -> list[str]:
        return [w for w in self.read(pid, "cmdline").decode("utf8", "replace").split("\0") if w]

    def cgroup(self, pid: int) -> str:
        for line in self.read(pid, "cgroup").decode("utf8", "replace").splitlines():
            if line.startswith("0::"):
                return line[3:]
        return ""

    def is_session_omp(self, pid: int, comm: str) -> bool:
        return comm == "omp" and not any("__omp_worker" in w for w in self.cmdline(pid)[:3])

    def environ(self, pid: int) -> dict:
        """The session a process's environment names: OMP_SESSION_ID and AGENT_SESSION_SCRATCH (omp
        sets both for every tool it runs, through its shared broker too). Unreadable for another
        uid, e.g. a box's processes."""
        found = {}
        for item in self.read(pid, "environ").split(b"\0"):
            for key, name in ((b"OMP_SESSION_ID=", "session"), (b"AGENT_SESSION_SCRATCH=", "scratch")):
                if item.startswith(key):
                    found[name] = item[len(key):].decode("utf8", "replace")
        return found

    def cwd(self, pid: int) -> str:
        try:
            return os.readlink(self.proc_root / str(pid) / "cwd")
        except OSError:
            return ""

    def scope_omps(self, scope: str, procs: dict) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:
        """(pid, start) of each session omp whose cgroup lies in `scope`; cgroups read once a sample."""
        if self._omp_cgroups is None:
            self._omp_cgroups = {(pid, row[2]): self.cgroup(pid) for pid, row in procs.items()
                                 if row[0] == "omp" and self.is_session_omp(pid, "omp")}
        return [key for key, cgroup in self._omp_cgroups.items() if scope in cgroup]

    def broker_env(self, unit: str, procs: dict) -> dict | None:
        """The environment of the omp broker of broker scope `unit` (any of its -N scopes), or None
        when no broker runs in it. A process the broker runs for nobody (a headless browser) carries
        this environment: the session that started the broker, not an owner."""
        base = BROKER_RE.match(unit)
        if not base:
            return None
        if self._brokers is None:
            self._brokers = {}
            for pid, row in procs.items():
                if row[0] == "omp daemon brok" or (row[0] == "omp" and "__omp_worker_daemon_broker" in self.cmdline(pid)[:3]):
                    found = BROKER_RE.match(self.cgroup(pid).rsplit("/", 1)[-1])
                    if found:
                        self._brokers[found[1]] = self.environ(pid)
        return self._brokers.get(base[1])

    # ---------------------------------------------------------------- sessions

    def session_of(self, pid: int, start: int, container: str = "", docker: bool = False) -> str:
        key = f"{pid}:{start}"
        cached = self.sessions.get(key)
        if cached and cached.get("session"):
            return cached["session"]
        found: set[str] = set()
        try:
            for fd in os.listdir(self.proc_root / str(pid) / "fd"):
                try:
                    match = TRANSCRIPT_RE.search(os.readlink(self.proc_root / str(pid) / "fd" / fd))
                except OSError:
                    continue
                if match:
                    found.add(match[1])
        except OSError:
            pass
        if not found:
            session = resume_session(self.cmdline(pid))
            if session:
                found.add(session)
        session = sorted(found)[0] if len(found) == 1 else ""
        if not session and docker and container:
            session = self.docker_session(container)
        if session:
            self.sessions[key] = {"session": session, "seen": time.time()}
        return session

    def owner_live(self, pid: int, procs: dict) -> dict:
        """What a live process tells of its owner, kept until its kill: the one session omp of its
        box or scope, its session omp ancestors (nearest first), its environment, working directory
        and scope unit. owner_of weighs them at the kill, when some may have gone."""
        cgroup = self.cgroup(pid)
        docker = DOCKER_RE.search(cgroup)
        container = docker[1] if docker else ""
        tree = []
        node, steps = procs.get(pid, (None, 0, 0, 0))[1], 0
        while node and node > 1 and steps < 64:
            row = procs.get(node) or self.stat(node)
            if not row:
                break
            if self.is_session_omp(node, row[0]):
                tree.append({"omp": node, "omp_start": row[2], "session": self.session_of(node, row[2], container)})
            node, steps = row[1], steps + 1
        scope_match = SCOPE_RE.match(cgroup)
        scope = docker[0] if docker else (scope_match[1] if scope_match else "")
        scope_omp = None
        if scope:
            owners = {key: self.session_of(key[0], key[1], container)
                      for key in self.scope_omps(scope, procs) if key[0] != pid}
            if len(set(owners.values())) == 1:
                (omp, omp_start), session = next(iter(owners.items()))
                scope_omp = {"omp": omp, "omp_start": omp_start, "session": session,
                             "how": "same agent box" if docker else "same systemd scope"}
        unit = scope.rsplit("/", 1)[-1] if not docker and re.search(r"/(?:run|omp-broker)-[^/]+\.scope$", scope) else ""
        entry = {"container": container, "cgroup": cgroup, "scope": unit, "scope_omp": scope_omp, "tree": tree,
                 "env": self.environ(pid), "cwd": self.cwd(pid)}
        if BROKER_RE.match(unit):
            entry["broker_env"] = self.broker_env(unit, procs)
        return entry

    # ---------------------------------------------------------------- sampling

    def sample(self, now: float) -> None:
        clock = time.monotonic()
        procs = self.scan()
        with self.lock:
            self.procs = procs
            self._omp_cgroups = self._brokers = None
            for pid, (comm, _ppid, start, rss) in procs.items():
                # omp and its broker are the sessions themselves, and earlyoom's --ignore spares them.
                if rss < RSS_FLOOR or comm in ("omp", "omp daemon brok"):
                    continue
                key = f"{pid}:{start}"
                entry = self.table.get(key)
                if entry is None:
                    entry = {"pid": pid, "start": start, "comm": comm, "first_seen": now, "rss_max": 0}
                    entry.update(self.owner_live(pid, procs))
                    self.table[key] = entry
                entry["last_seen"] = now
                entry["rss_max"] = max(entry["rss_max"], rss >> 20)
            for key in [k for k, e in self.table.items() if now - e.get("last_seen", 0) > KEEP_DEAD]:
                del self.table[key]
            for key in [k for k, e in self.sessions.items() if now - e.get("seen", 0) > 86400]:
                del self.sessions[key]
        self.sample_ms = int((time.monotonic() - clock) * 1000)

    # ---------------------------------------------------------------- journal

    def hour(self, epoch: float) -> dict:
        return self.hours.setdefault(hour_key(epoch), {"kills": 0, "unmatched": 0, "notices": 0})

    def on_entry(self, entry: dict, now: float) -> None:
        cursor = entry.get("__CURSOR") or ""
        ts_us = int(entry.get("__REALTIME_TIMESTAMP") or 0)
        with self.lock:
            if ts_us < self.last_ts or (cursor and cursor in self.recent):
                return
            self.last_ts, self.cursor = ts_us, cursor or self.cursor
            self.recent = (self.recent + [cursor])[-64:]
            message = message_of(entry)
            avail = parse_avail(message)
            if avail:
                self.avail = list(avail)
                return
            kill = parse_kill(message)
            if not kill:
                return
            at = ts_us / 1e6
            kill["at"] = at
            kill["avail"] = self.avail
            self.hour(at)["kills"] += 1
            owner = self.owner_of(kill)
            kill.update(how=owner["how"], omp=owner["omp"], session=owner["session"])
            if owner.get("unknown"):
                kill["unknown"] = owner["unknown"]
            # The box-level rate counts every kill, matched or not. A storm from before a first
            # start is counted, not sent, like the per-session notices.
            notify = at >= self.notify_after
            self.box_step(at, notify)  # a fall to the threshold before this kill closes the storm
            self.box_kills.append([at, owner["session"], kill["comm"], kill["rss_mib"]])
            self.box_step(at, notify)
            if not owner["session"]:
                self.hour(at)["unmatched"] += 1
                if not owner.get("unknown"):
                    log(f"{utc(at)} unmatched kill: pid {kill['pid']} uid {kill['uid']} \"{kill['comm']}\""
                        f" {kill['rss_mib']} MiB: {kill['cmdline'][:160]}")
                    return
                log(f"{utc(at)} kill: pid {kill['pid']} \"{kill['comm']}\" {kill['rss_mib']} MiB -> box-health owner,"
                    f" owner unknown ({owner['unknown']}): {kill['cmdline'][:160]}")
            else:
                log(f"{utc(at)} kill: pid {kill['pid']} \"{kill['comm']}\" {kill['rss_mib']} MiB -> session"
                    f" {owner['session']} ({owner['how']})")
            if at < self.notify_after or (not self.replay and now - at > STALE):
                return
            # Kills of no known owner are one batch, session "", for the box-health owner.
            for batch in self.pending:
                if batch["session"] == owner["session"] and at - batch["opened"] < BATCH:
                    batch["kills"].append(kill)
                    break
            else:
                self.pending.append({"session": owner["session"], "opened": at, "kills": [kill], "retry_at": 0})

    def live_here(self) -> dict[str, str]:
        now = time.monotonic()
        if now - self._live_at >= LIVE_TTL:
            self._live, self._live_at = self.live() or {}, now
        return self._live

    def live_omp_session(self, rec: dict | None, container: str = "") -> str:
        """The session of a recorded omp that still runs (same pid and start time), else ""."""
        if not rec or not rec.get("omp"):
            return ""
        omp = self.stat(rec["omp"])
        if not omp or omp[2] != rec.get("omp_start"):
            return ""
        if not rec.get("session"):
            rec["session"] = self.session_of(rec["omp"], omp[2], container, docker=True)
        return rec["session"]

    def tmp_session(self, text: str) -> tuple[str, int]:
        """(session, omp pid) from a `session-tmp/<omp pid>-XXXXXXXX` path whose omp still runs."""
        match = SESSION_TMP_RE.search(text + " ")
        if match:
            omp_pid = int(match[1])
            omp = self.stat(omp_pid)
            if omp and omp[0] == "omp":
                return self.session_of(omp_pid, omp[2]), omp_pid
        return "", 0

    def path_session(self, text: str) -> str:
        """A live-here session that a path names: its full id, or a `<Name>-<8 hex>` directory when
        exactly one live-here session id starts with those 8 hex."""
        ids = {m[1] for m in SESSION_UUID_RE.finditer(text)}
        prefixes = {m[1] for m in SESSION_DIR_RE.finditer(text)}
        if not ids and not prefixes:
            return ""
        live = self.live_here()
        found = ids & set(live)
        if not found:
            for prefix in prefixes:
                found |= {s for s in live if s.startswith(prefix)}
        return found.pop() if len(found) == 1 else ""

    def cgroup_session(self, cgroup: str, pid: int) -> str:
        """The one live-here session every other readable process of `cgroup` names in its environment."""
        if not cgroup:
            return ""
        found = set()
        for other in self.procs:
            if other != pid and self.cgroup(other) == cgroup:
                session = self.environ(other).get("session")
                if session:
                    found.add(session)
        return found.pop() if len(found) == 1 and next(iter(found)) in self.live_here() else ""

    def scope_session(self, unit: str) -> tuple[str, str]:
        """(session, rule) a scope names: a `-svc` scope's Description `omp session <uuid>` (step 3),
        else the original session of a `run-*.scope` (step 4); the session may have moved or ended."""
        if not unit.startswith("run-"):
            return "", ""
        description = self.describe(unit)
        named = DESCRIPTION_RE.match(description)
        run_c = RUN_C_RE.match(unit)
        if run_c and run_c[2]:
            return (named[1], f"its systemd scope {unit}, whose Description names the session") if named else ("", "")
        if named:
            return named[1], f"its systemd scope {unit}, made for this session (no omp runs in it now)"
        found = {resume_session(description.split())} - {""}
        if len(found) == 1:
            return found.pop(), f"its systemd scope {unit}, which shims/omp started for this session (no omp runs in it now)"
        if run_c:
            hex16 = run_c[1]
            ids = {s for s in self.live_here() if s.replace("-", "").startswith(hex16)}
            if len(ids) == 1:
                return ids.pop(), f"its systemd scope {unit}, named for this session (no omp runs in it now)"
            return f"{hex16[:8]}-{hex16[8:12]}-{hex16[12:]}…", ""
        return "", ""

    def owner_of(self, kill: dict) -> dict:
        """The session to tell, in the order of the module's doc. A session that has moved off this
        host or ended is never told: such a kill goes to the box-health owner as "owner unknown"."""
        pid, comm = kill["pid"], kill["comm"]
        # earlyoom logs before it signals, so the process is sometimes still here. Not in a replay:
        # by then the pid may be another process with the same name.
        row = None if self.replay else self.stat(pid)
        if row and row[0] == comm:
            entry = self.table.get(f"{pid}:{row[2]}")
            if entry is None:
                self._omp_cgroups = self._brokers = None
                entry = self.owner_live(pid, self.scan())
            elif not entry.get("env"):
                entry["env"] = self.environ(pid)
        else:
            known = [e for e in self.table.values() if e["pid"] == pid and e["comm"] == comm]
            entry = max(known, key=lambda e: e.get("last_seen", 0)) if known else {}
        container = entry.get("container", "")
        # `envoy ps` takes seconds, so it is read only past the omp rules (most kills stop there).
        # 1. the scope's live omp
        scope_omp = entry.get("scope_omp")
        session = self.live_omp_session(scope_omp, container)
        if session:
            ancestor = any(r.get("omp") == scope_omp["omp"] for r in entry.get("tree") or [])
            return {"session": session, "how": "process tree" if ancestor else scope_omp["how"], "omp": scope_omp["omp"]}
        # 2. the process: its nearest live omp ancestor, its environment, its cgroup's, its paths
        for rec in entry.get("tree") or []:
            session = self.live_omp_session(rec, container)
            if session:
                return {"session": session, "how": "process tree", "omp": rec["omp"]}
        env = entry.get("env") or {}
        unit = entry.get("scope", "")
        broker = bool(BROKER_RE.match(unit))
        inherited = ""
        if broker and (env.get("session") or env.get("scratch")):
            # A process the broker runs for nobody carries the broker's own environment: the session
            # that started the broker, not an owner. With no broker to compare, nothing is known.
            broker_env = entry.get("broker_env")
            name = "session" if env.get("session") else "scratch"
            if broker_env is None or broker_env.get(name) == env[name]:
                inherited, env = env[name], {}
        if env.get("session") and env["session"] in self.live_here():
            return {"session": env["session"], "how": "its environment (OMP_SESSION_ID)", "omp": 0}
        session, omp_pid = self.tmp_session(env.get("scratch", ""))
        if session:
            return {"session": session, "how": "its environment (AGENT_SESSION_SCRATCH)", "omp": omp_pid}
        # The processes of a broker scope serve many sessions: no one of them speaks for another.
        if not env.get("session") and not broker and not inherited:
            session = self.cgroup_session(entry.get("cgroup", ""), pid)
            if session:
                return {"session": session, "how": "the environment of the other processes of its cgroup", "omp": 0}
        session, omp_pid = self.tmp_session(kill["cmdline"])
        if session:
            return {"session": session, "how": "session-tmp path in its command line", "omp": omp_pid}
        for where, text in (("command line", kill["cmdline"]), ("working directory", entry.get("cwd", ""))):
            session = self.path_session(text)
            if session:
                return {"session": session, "how": f"a session's directory in its {where}", "omp": 0}
        # 3. and 4. what its scope names, only when that session is live here
        session, how = self.scope_session(unit)
        if session and session in self.live_here():
            return {"session": session, "how": how, "omp": 0}
        if unit.startswith("omp-broker-"):
            why = f"it ran in {unit}, the omp broker scope several sessions share, and named no live session"
        elif session:
            why = f"it ran in {unit}, whose session {session} has moved off this host or ended"
        elif unit:
            why = f"it ran in {unit}, which names no session"
        elif container:
            why = f"it ran in agent box {container[:12]}, whose omp no longer runs"
        else:
            return {"session": "", "how": "", "omp": 0}
        if env.get("session"):
            why += f"; its environment names session {env['session']}, not live on this host"
        if inherited:
            why += (f"; its environment names {inherited}, which is the broker's own (the session that"
                    " started the broker, not an owner)" if entry.get("broker_env") is not None else
                    f"; its environment names {inherited}, and no broker runs in the scope to tell that from"
                    " the broker's own")
        return {"session": "", "how": "", "omp": 0, "unknown": why}

    # ---------------------------------------------------------------- the box-level rate

    def box_rate(self, t: float, since: float = 0.0) -> int:
        """Kills in the hour to `t`, or only those after `since` when that is later."""
        lo = max(t - BOX_WINDOW, since)
        return sum(1 for k in self.box_kills if lo < k[0] <= t)

    def box_step(self, t: float, notify: bool = True) -> None:
        """Judge the box-level rate at time `t`: open a storm over BOX_RATE kills in the hour, tell
        it again only when twice as many kills as last told came since, and close it, silently,
        once the hour's count is back at BOX_RATE, so the next crossing is news."""
        with self.lock:
            self.box_kills = [k for k in self.box_kills if k[0] > t - 2 * BOX_WINDOW]
            rate = self.box_rate(t)
            box = self.box
            if box.get("open"):
                if rate <= BOX_RATE:
                    log(f"{utc(t)} box kill rate back to {rate} in the hour (at most {BOX_RATE}): storm closed")
                    self.box = {"open": False, "closed_at": t}
                    return
                since = self.box_rate(t, box["told_at"])
                if since < 2 * box["told"]:
                    return
                due = {"kind": "doubled", "count": since, "prev": box["told"], "prev_at": box["told_at"]}
                box.update(told=since, told_at=t)
            elif rate > BOX_RATE:
                due = {"kind": "crossed", "count": rate}
                self.box = {"open": True, "opened_at": t, "told": rate, "told_at": t}
            else:
                return
            log(f"{utc(t)} box kill rate {rate} in the hour: {due['kind']}{'' if notify else ' (before start: counted, not sent)'}")
            if not notify:
                return
            due.update(rate=rate, at=t, retry_at=0)
            pending = self.box_pending
            if pending and not pending.get("sending"):
                # The last message was never delivered: this one replaces it and tells what it would
                # have, counted to now, and the next "doubled" is judged against what this one tells.
                if pending["kind"] == "crossed":
                    due.update(kind="crossed", count=rate)
                else:
                    due.update(kind="doubled", prev=pending["prev"], prev_at=pending["prev_at"],
                               count=self.box_rate(t, pending["prev_at"]))
                self.box.update(told=due["count"], told_at=t)
            self.box_pending = due

    def box_text(self, due: dict, report: str) -> str:
        at, rate = due["at"], due["rate"]
        window = [k for k in self.box_kills if at - BOX_WINDOW < k[0] <= at]
        sessions = {k[1] for k in window if k[1]}
        unmatched = sum(1 for k in window if not k[1])
        top = ", ".join(f"{comm} {n}" for comm, n in Counter(k[2] for k in window).most_common(3))
        free = meminfo_available(self.proc_root).split(" ")[0]
        if due["kind"] == "doubled":
            what = (f"rate doubled: {due['count']} kills since the last message at {utc(due['prev_at'])},"
                    f" which told {due['prev']}; {rate} in the hour to {utc(at)}")
        else:
            what = f"{rate} kills in the hour to {utc(at)}, over {BOX_RATE}"
        text = (
            ("DRILL COPY of the box-level message (--to). " if self.to else "")
            + f"EARLYOOM KILL RATE on {self.host}: {what}."
            + (f" Memory available now {free}." if free else "")
            + f" Box-health owner: find what holds the memory and slow it. {len(sessions)} sessions were told of"
            f" their own kills; {unmatched} kills had no session. Most killed: {top}. Said again only when"
            f" {2 * due['count']} more come within an hour, or after the hour's count falls to {BOX_RATE}"
            " and crosses again. "
        )
        return bounded(text, f"Full report: {report}")

    def box_report(self, due: dict) -> str:
        at, rate = due["at"], due["rate"]
        window = [k for k in self.box_kills if at - BOX_WINDOW < k[0] <= at]
        by_comm: dict[str, list[int]] = {}
        for _t, _session, comm, rss in window:
            row = by_comm.setdefault(comm, [0, 0])
            row[0] += 1
            row[1] += rss
        sessions = Counter(k[1] for k in window if k[1])
        unmatched = sum(1 for k in window if not k[1])
        lines = [
            f"earlyoom-kill-watch on {self.host}, {utc(at)}: box-level earlyoom kill rate, {due['kind']}.",
            f"{rate} kills in the hour to {utc(at)} (more than {BOX_RATE} is a storm)."
            + (f" {due['count']} of them came after the last message at {utc(due['prev_at'])}, which told"
               f" {due['prev']}." if due["kind"] == "doubled" else ""),
            f"Host available memory now: {meminfo_available(self.proc_root) or 'not readable'}.",
            "",
            "Kills by command in that hour (count, summed VmRSS at the kill):",
        ]
        lines += [f"  {comm} {n} kills, {rss} MiB" for comm, (n, rss) in
                  sorted(by_comm.items(), key=lambda item: -item[1][0])[:20]]
        lines += ["", f"Sessions told of their own kills ({len(sessions)}; each had its own notice):"]
        lines += [f"  {session} {n} kills" for session, n in sessions.most_common(30)]
        lines += [f"{unmatched} kills had no session (system services, containers outside a box, processes"
                  " younger than one 2 s sample, or left behind by a session that moved or ended): no session was"
                  " told of them; those left in a session's scope came to the box-health owner as owner unknown.",
                  "", "Kills per clock hour (this watch's count):"]
        lines += [f"  {hour} {row.get('kills', 0)} kills, {row.get('unmatched', 0)} unmatched"
                  for hour, row in sorted(self.hours.items())[-6:]]
        lines += [
            "",
            "What to do: find the sessions that hold the memory now and slow them, e.g. `session-cpu-record top"
            " --since 1h` (sessions by cores and peak RSS), `journalctl -u earlyoom --since -1h` (each kill),"
            " `earlyoom-kill-watch --counts` (kills per hour). The kills themselves keep the omp sessions alive.",
            f"Said again only when {2 * due['count']} more kills come within an hour of this message, or after the"
            f" hour's count falls to {BOX_RATE} and crosses again. Nothing is sent when it falls.",
        ]
        return "\n".join(lines) + "\n"

    # ---------------------------------------------------------------- notices

    def notice(self, batch: dict, report: str) -> str:
        if not batch["session"]:
            return self.unknown_notice(batch, report)
        kills = batch["kills"]
        free = meminfo_available(self.proc_root).split(" ")[0]
        head = (
            (f"DRILL COPY for session {batch['session']} (--to). " if self.to else "")
            + f"earlyoom on {self.host} stopped {len(kills)} of your processes (SIGTERM, host memory at 10%): "
        )
        advice = (
            ". They exit 143 with no message; not a fault in your work. Before a rerun: run fewer jobs at once"
            " or with less memory, or run it as a dispatch-cluster Job (skill://running-heavy-jobs)."
            + (f" Memory available now {free}." if free else "") + " "
        )
        tail = f"Full report: {report}"
        items = [f"{utc(k['at'])} pid {k['pid']} \"{k['comm']}\" {k['rss_mib']} MiB" for k in kills]
        return bounded(head + listed(items, MESSAGE_LIMIT - len(head) - len(advice) - len(tail)) + advice, tail)

    def unknown_notice(self, batch: dict, report: str) -> str:
        """Kills of no live owner, for the box-health owner: each command line, as many as fit."""
        kills = batch["kills"]
        head = (
            ("DRILL COPY of the owner-unknown notice (--to). " if self.to else "")
            + f"OWNER UNKNOWN: earlyoom on {self.host} stopped {len(kills)} processes (SIGTERM, host memory at 10%)"
            " whose session is not live on this host (it moved or ended), so no session was told."
            " Box-health owner: find who runs them; stop them if nobody does. "
        )
        tail = f" Full report: {report}"
        items = [f"{utc(k['at'])} pid {k['pid']} {k['rss_mib']} MiB: {k['cmdline'][:120]}" for k in kills]
        return bounded(head + listed(items, MESSAGE_LIMIT - len(head) - len(tail)), tail)

    def notice_report(self, batch: dict) -> str:
        kills = batch["kills"]
        lines = []
        for kill in kills:
            avail = kill.get("avail")
            memory = f"host available memory {avail[2]:.2f}% ({avail[0]} of {avail[1]} MiB)" if avail else \
                "host available memory not logged"
            lines.append(
                f"- {utc(kill['at'])}: pid {kill['pid']} \"{kill['comm']}\", VmRSS {kill['rss_mib']} MiB,"
                f" {memory}. Command: {kill['cmdline'][:2000]}"
            )
        hows = sorted({f"{k['how']} (omp pid {k['omp']})" if k["omp"] else k["how"] for k in kills})
        now_free = meminfo_available(self.proc_root)
        if not batch["session"]:
            whys = sorted({k.get("unknown", "") for k in kills})
            return (
                f"earlyoom-kill-watch on {self.host}: OWNER UNKNOWN. The host's earlyoom stopped {len(kills)}"
                " processes with SIGTERM, because the host's available memory fell to 10%. No live session on"
                " this host owns them, so no session was told; a session that moved or ended is never told.\n"
                + "\n".join(lines)
                + "\nWhy no owner: " + "; ".join(whys) + ".\n"
                "Box-health owner: find who runs these commands (the paths often name the session) and tell"
                " them, or stop the work if nobody owns it."
                + (f" Available now: {now_free}." if now_free else "") + "\n"
            )
        return (
            f"earlyoom-kill-watch on {self.host}: the host's earlyoom stopped {len(kills)} processes of session"
            f" {batch['session']} with SIGTERM, because the host's available memory fell to 10%.\n"
            + "\n".join(lines)
            + "\nA tool that earlyoom stopped exits with status 143 and gives no message. The kill keeps the"
            " omp sessions on this host alive; it is not a fault in your tool or your work.\n"
            "Before you run it again, do one of these: (1) run fewer of these jobs in parallel, or give"
            " each one less memory; (2) run a large build, test suite, eval or sweep as a Job in the"
            " dispatch cluster (skill://running-heavy-jobs); (3) wait until the host's available memory"
            " is well above 10% (`grep MemAvailable /proc/meminfo`), then try again."
            + (f" Available now: {now_free}." if now_free else "")
            + f"\nMatched to the session by: {'; '.join(hows)}. (An automated notice, not a person;"
            " one notice per minute of kills.)\n"
        )

    def write_report(self, kind: str, text: str, now: float) -> str:
        """Write one report file and prune those older than REPORT_DAYS; its path, or why there is none."""
        stamp = time.strftime("%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ", time.gmtime(now))
        path = self.reports_dir / f"{stamp}-{kind}.txt"
        try:
            self.reports_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
            n = 2
            while path.exists():
                path, n = self.reports_dir / f"{stamp}-{kind}-{n}.txt", n + 1
            path.write_text(text)
        except OSError as error:
            log(f"report {path} not written: {error}")
            return f"none ({path} not written: {error.strerror or error})"
        cutoff = now - REPORT_DAYS * 86400
        for old in self.reports_dir.glob("*.txt"):
            try:
                if old.stat().st_mtime < cutoff:
                    old.unlink()
            except OSError:
                continue
        return str(path)

    def flush(self, now: float, force: bool = False) -> int:
        with self.lock:
            due = [b for b in self.pending
                   if (force or now - b["opened"] >= BATCH) and now >= b.get("retry_at", 0) and not b.get("sending")]
            for batch in due:
                batch["sending"] = True
            box = self.box_pending
            if box and (box.get("sending") or now < box.get("retry_at", 0)):
                box = None
            if box:
                box["sending"] = True
        sent = 0
        for batch in due:
            # Kills of no live owner go to the box-health owner: its role, else the SRE session.
            targets = [self.to] if self.to else [batch["session"]] if batch["session"] else [BOX_HEALTH_ROLE_TOPIC, SRE]
            # Written once per batch: a retry names the same report.
            if not batch.get("report"):
                kind = f"notice-{batch['session'][:8]}" if batch["session"] else "owner-unknown"
                batch["report"] = self.write_report(kind, self.notice_report(batch), now)
            text = self.notice(batch, batch["report"])
            target = next((t for t in targets if self.send(t, text)), "")
            ok = bool(target)
            with self.lock:
                batch.pop("sending", None)
                if ok:
                    self.pending.remove(batch)
                    self.hour(now)["notices"] += 1
                    sent += 1
                    log(f"notice sent to {target}: {len(batch['kills'])} kill(s) of"
                        f" {('session ' + batch['session']) if batch['session'] else 'no live owner (owner unknown)'}")
                else:
                    batch["retry_at"] = now + RETRY
        if box:
            sent += self.send_box(box, now)
        return sent

    def send_box(self, box: dict, now: float) -> int:
        if not box.get("report"):
            box["report"] = self.write_report("box-rate", self.box_report(box), now)
        text = self.box_text(box, box["report"])
        told = next((t for t in ([self.to] if self.to else [BOX_HEALTH_ROLE_TOPIC, SRE]) if self.send(t, text)), "")
        with self.lock:
            box.pop("sending", None)
            if not told:
                box["retry_at"] = now + RETRY
                return 0
            if self.box_pending is box:
                self.box_pending = None
            log(f"box-level message sent to {told}: {box['rate']} kills in the hour ({box['kind']})")
            return 1

    def counts_line(self, now: float) -> str:
        with self.lock:
            this = self.hours.get(hour_key(now), {})
            prev = self.hours.get(hour_key(now - 3600), {})
            return (
                f"kills_this_hour={this.get('kills', 0)} hour={hour_key(now)} kills_prev_hour={prev.get('kills', 0)}"
                f" unmatched_this_hour={this.get('unmatched', 0)} notices_this_hour={this.get('notices', 0)}"
                f" tracked={len(self.table)} pending={len(self.pending)} sample_ms={self.sample_ms}"
                f" box_rate_1h={self.box_rate(now)}"
            )

    def save(self, now: float) -> None:
        if self.replay:
            return
        with self.lock:
            for key in sorted(self.hours)[:-HOURS_KEPT]:
                del self.hours[key]
            state = {
                "cursor": self.cursor, "last_ts": self.last_ts, "recent": self.recent, "table": self.table,
                "sessions": self.sessions, "hours": self.hours, "avail": self.avail,
                "pending": [{k: v for k, v in b.items() if k != "sending"} for b in self.pending],
                "box_kills": self.box_kills, "box": self.box,
                "box_pending": {k: v for k, v in self.box_pending.items() if k != "sending"} if self.box_pending else None,
                "saved_at": utc(now),
            }
            self.state_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
            tmp = self.state_path.with_suffix(".tmp")
            tmp.write_text(json.dumps(state))
            tmp.replace(self.state_path)


def journal_args(watch: Watch, now: float, since: str = "", until: str = "", follow: bool = True) -> list[str]:
    args = ["journalctl", "-u", "earlyoom", "-o", "json", "--no-pager"]
    if since:
        args.append(f"--since={since}")
    elif watch.cursor:
        args.append(f"--after-cursor={watch.cursor}")
    else:
        args.append(f"--since=@{int(now // 3600 * 3600)}")
    if until:
        args.append(f"--until={until}")
    if follow:
        args.append("--follow")
    return args


def journal_time(text: str) -> str:
    """`2026-11-02T15:00Z` -> what journalctl takes (`2026-11-02 15:00:00 UTC`)."""
    match = re.fullmatch(r"(\d{4}-\d\d-\d\d)[T ](\d\d:\d\d)(?::(\d\d))?Z?", text)
    return f"{match[1]} {match[2]}:{match[3] or '00'} UTC" if match else text


def run_service(options: argparse.Namespace) -> int:
    lock_path = options.state.with_suffix(".lock")
    lock_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    lock = open(lock_path, "w")
    try:
        fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
    except OSError:
        log(f"another earlyoom-kill-watch holds {lock_path}; exiting")
        return 1
    send = envoy_send
    if options.dry_run:
        def send(target, text):
            log(f"DRY RUN: would send to {target}: {text}")
            return True
    now = time.time()
    watch = Watch(state_path=options.state, send=send, to=options.to, started=now, reports_dir=options.reports)
    lines: queue.Queue = queue.Queue()
    journal = subprocess.Popen(journal_args(watch, now), stdout=subprocess.PIPE, text=True, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)

    def read_journal() -> None:
        for raw in journal.stdout:
            lines.put(raw)
        lines.put(None)

    threading.Thread(target=read_journal, daemon=True).start()
    sender: threading.Thread | None = None
    log(f"earlyoom-kill-watch started: state {options.state}, reports {options.reports},"
        f" route {'--to ' + options.to if options.to else 'owner; box rate to ' + BOX_HEALTH_ROLE_TOPIC},"
        f" {'from cursor' if watch.cursor else 'no cursor: counting from the hour, notifying from now'}")
    last_report = 0.0

    def send_due(at: float) -> None:
        if watch.flush(at):
            watch.save(time.time())

    # systemd stops the service with SIGTERM; the state is saved on the way out, so a restart
    # neither counts nor sends a line twice.
    signal.signal(signal.SIGTERM, lambda *_: sys.exit(0))
    try:
        while True:
            now = time.time()
            watch.sample(now)
            read = 0
            while True:
                try:
                    raw = lines.get_nowait()
                except queue.Empty:
                    break
                if raw is None:
                    log(f"journalctl exited ({journal.wait()}); exiting for systemd to restart")
                    return 1
                try:
                    watch.on_entry(json.loads(raw), now)
                except ValueError:
                    continue
                read += 1
            if read:
                watch.save(now)
            watch.box_step(now)  # the hour's count also falls with no kill at all
            if (watch.pending or watch.box_pending) and (sender is None or not sender.is_alive()):
                sender = threading.Thread(target=send_due, args=(now,), daemon=True)
                sender.start()
            if now - last_report >= 60:
                log(watch.counts_line(now))
                watch.save(now)
                last_report = now
            time.sleep(max(0.2, SAMPLE_EVERY - (time.time() - now)))
    finally:
        watch.save(time.time())
        journal.terminate()


def run_replay(options: argparse.Namespace) -> int:
    """Read a past window of the journal and show whom each kill would reach, with what this
    watch knows now (its saved table and the live process tree). Sends only with --send."""
    def show(target, text):
        log(f"WOULD SEND to {target}:\n{text}\n")
        return True

    watch = Watch(state_path=options.state, send=envoy_send if options.send else show, to=options.to, replay=True,
                  reports_dir=options.reports)
    watch.cursor, watch.last_ts, watch.recent, watch.pending = None, 0, [], []
    watch.hours, watch.box_kills, watch.box, watch.box_pending = {}, [], {}, None
    watch.sample(time.time())
    args = journal_args(watch, time.time(), since=journal_time(options.since),
                        until=journal_time(options.until) if options.until else "", follow=False)
    done = subprocess.run(args, capture_output=True, text=True)
    for raw in done.stdout.splitlines():
        try:
            watch.on_entry(json.loads(raw), time.time())
        except ValueError:
            continue
    watch.flush(time.time(), force=True)
    log(json.dumps(watch.hours, sort_keys=True))
    return 0


def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.splitlines()[0])
    parser.add_argument("--to", default="", help="send every notice to this session id instead of its owner (a drill)")
    parser.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true", help="log the notices; send nothing")
    parser.add_argument("--state", type=Path, default=DEFAULT_STATE)
    parser.add_argument("--reports", type=Path, default=DEFAULT_REPORTS,
                        help="where each message's full report goes (pruned after 7 days)")
    parser.add_argument("--replay", action="store_true", help="read a past window; send nothing unless --send")
    parser.add_argument("--since", default="", help="replay window start, e.g. 2026-11-02T15:00Z")
    parser.add_argument("--until", default="", help="replay window end")
    parser.add_argument("--send", action="store_true", help="with --replay: send the notices")
    parser.add_argument("--counts", action="store_true", help="print the saved kills per hour as JSON")
    options = parser.parse_args(argv)
    if options.to and not re.fullmatch(UUID, options.to):
        parser.error(f"--to {options.to!r} is not a session id")
    if options.counts:
        try:
            print(json.dumps(json.loads(options.state.read_text()).get("hours") or {}, indent=1, sort_keys=True))
        except (OSError, ValueError) as error:
            print(f"no state at {options.state}: {error}", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        return 0
    if options.replay:
        if not options.since:
            parser.error("--replay needs --since")
        return run_replay(options)
    return run_service(options)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
